  "description": "bit Bsqlite: SQLite in the browser for Blazor, with EF Core on top. The ADO.NET surface with live queries, the worker transport (storage selection, engine-build negotiation, binary framing, batching, lifecycle), the storage provider contract, the EF Core integration (UseBitBsqlite() on the stock SQLite provider), the storage backends - OPFS (OPFSCoopSyncVFS), IndexedDB (IDBBatchAtomicVFS), Cache Storage (which imports a database Bit.Besql left behind) and in-memory - and the browser half: worker host, wa-sqlite engine builds and VFSes, each downloaded only when the backend that needs it is selected.",
  "iconFile": "PackageIcon.png",
